lesson: 209
title: People and animals together
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A person walks on 2 legs, while a dog, a cat or a sheep walks on 4.
explain: Do not forget the people when you count legs: a dog walker with 4 dogs makes 2 + 4 × 4 = 18 legs.
explain: When someone says «me and my 5 friends», that is 6 people. 6 people and 2 dogs: 6 × 2 + 2 × 4 = 12 + 8 = 20 legs.
vars: a=name b=name p=3..9 d=2..6
let: q = p - 1
answer: 2 * p + 4 * d
exercise: {p} hikers walk up a hill with {d} dogs. How many legs go up the hill?
exercise: {p} children sit on the sofa with {d} cats. How many legs are on the sofa?
exercise: {a} and {q} friends take {d} dogs to the beach. How many legs walk on the sand?
exercise: {p} farmers stand in a field with {d} sheep. How many legs are in the field?
exercise: At a party there are {p} children and {d} dogs. How many legs are there at the party?
exercise: {a} walks {d} dogs with {q} other dog walkers. How many legs is that, people and dogs together?
exercise: me and my {q} mates n {d} dogs on the hike. how many legs counting us
exercise: {p} kids and {d} cats on the sofa, nobody's doing homework lol. legs?
exercise: {q+2}, no wait, {q} friends came round plus me, and {d} dogs. how many legs in the house
exercise: {b} says it's {4*d} legs cos {d} dogs, forgot the {p} walkers lol. legs really?
exercise: dog walker gang: {p} people, {d} dogs, it was raining heaps. how many legs
test: Count the people's and the animals' legs: {d} sheep and the {p} farmers watching them.
test: {d} dogs follow {p} children home from school. How many legs come through the door?
test: I went to the park with my {q} cousins and our {d} dogs. How many legs did we take to the park, mine included?
test: What is the number of legs on {p} people and {d} cats in the kitchen?
test: me n {q} others walkin {d} dogs. legs incl me?
test: party: {p} kids, {d} dogs, one massive cake. legs all up
exam: Determine the aggregate number of legs pertaining to {p.words} persons accompanied by {d.words} dogs.
exam: It is given that the speaker, together with {q} companions, conducts {d} sheep across a field. Ascertain the total quantity of legs, the speaker's included.
exam: A gathering comprises {p} children and {d} cats. Compute the number of legs belonging to all those present.
exam: Whereas {d} dogs are exercised by {p} walkers, state the combined number of legs of walkers and dogs alike.
exercise: {p} hikers set off with {d+1} dogs, but the oldest dog is 'no spring chicken' and stayed in the car. How many legs go up the hill?
exercise: Since Gran passed away, her {d} cats live with {a}'s family of {p}. They all squeeze onto the sofa. How many legs are on the sofa?
test: {p} of us n {d+1} dogs on the walk, one dog's 'big-boned' n gave up, we left it tied up at the pub. how many legs still walking
